---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CRITERIA } from '../lib/score.mjs';
---
<Page title="How We Score Products – The RenterSmartHome Score" description="How the RenterSmartHome Score works: five renter criteria, their weights, the formula and what each number means." updated="October 15, 2026">
  <p>Every product we recommend gets a <strong>RenterSmartHome Spec Score</strong> out of 5. It answers one question: <em>how well does this product work for someone who rents?</em> It's our own editorial rating, built from manufacturer specifications, installation manuals and the research listed in each guide. It is not a customer rating, and we never copy star ratings from stores.</p>

  <h2>The five criteria</h2>
  <p>We rate each product from 1 to 10 on five criteria, weighted by how much they matter to renters:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Criterion</th><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">What a 10 looks like</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {CRITERIA.map((c) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{c.label}</td>
          <td>{Math.round(c.weight * 100)}%</td>
          <td>{{
            install: 'Plugs in, stands up or sticks on. No tools, drilling or wiring.',
            reversibility: 'Comes out in minutes and leaves nothing behind on move-out day.',
            value: 'Fair price for what it does, with no subscription needed for the core features.',
            compatibility: 'Works with Matter and all major assistants (Alexa, Google Home, Apple Home).',
            portability: 'Fits any apartment and works the same in your next one.',
          }[c.key]}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>The formula</h2>
  <p><strong>Score = (Install × 30% + Reversibility × 25% + Value × 20% + Compatibility × 15% + Portability × 10%) ÷ 2</strong>, rounded to one decimal.</p>
  <p>Some criteria don't apply to every product. An adhesive hook or a baby gate has no smart home compatibility, so we leave that criterion out and rescale the other weights so they still add up to 100%. That keeps non-smart products from being punished for something they were never meant to do.</p>

  <h2>How we pick each number</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Install footprint:</strong> 10 plug-in or freestanding · 9 adhesive or tension mount · 8 swaps an existing part without tools · 7 screwdriver retrofit · 5-6 leaves a small hole · 2-4 needs wiring, HVAC access or an electrician.</li>
    <li><strong>Reversibility:</strong> 10 unplug and go · 9 peel off or release tension · 8 reinstall the original part · 6 a pinhole to fill · 3 or lower needs a professional to restore.</li>
    <li><strong>Value and subscriptions:</strong> 10 low cost with nothing to pay monthly · 8 good value · 6 premium price, or a paid plan needed for important features.</li>
    <li><strong>Smart home compatibility:</strong> 10 Matter plus every major platform · 8-9 two or three platforms · 6-7 mainly one ecosystem.</li>
    <li><strong>Portability:</strong> 10 works anywhere · 8 depends on fit (deadbolt, door, window) · 6 made to measure · 5 or lower tied to the building's systems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the score is not</h2>
  <p>It is a spec-based score, not a measurement: we haven't had these products in hand, so each criterion is judged from published figures (for example load rating, materials, lock type, size and weight) and from owner reports, never from our own tests. It isn't a lab test or a customer review average, and it doesn't change with price swings or sales. When a product, its app or its subscription changes, we re-check it and update the score. Read more about our <a href="/how-we-research/">research process</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
</Page>
